# Plan (opus, strong)

**Goal.** When an unranked match is over, each watcher on `/ws/watch` is still sent every delayed view it is owed, oldest first, through the view that shows the result. Once it has had that last view, its socket closes with 1000 and the reason `the match is over`, it leaves `core.spectate.watchers` (so `watcher_count` drops), and both players' sockets get a `watchers` frame with the new count. A void still closes every watcher at once with `MATCH_VOIDED_CLOSE_CODE` (that is 4410; the issue's "4404" is wrong), because that path is not touched. The spec does not say when a watch ends, so this is a new ruling, R1107000 (the first number in issue #1107's block).

**Files to touch.**

| File | new/change | What |
|---|---|---|
| `crates/server/src/actor/match_actor.rs` | change | const `MATCH_OVER_CLOSE_REASON`; free fn `close_finished_watchers`; method `MatchActor::spectate_let_go_finished`; calls to it in the wait's callback inside `spectate_flush` and twice in `attach_watcher`; section comment and `CLOSE_NORMAL` doc |
