   ```rust
   /// R1107000: closes the sockets of the watchers `MatchActor::spectate_let_go_finished` let go, each
   /// with CLOSE_NORMAL. Called without the actor's lock, which each socket's close handler takes; the
   /// handler finds its watcher already out of the list.
   fn close_finished_watchers(watchers: Vec<Watcher>) {
       for watcher in watchers {
           if watcher.socket.is_open() {
               watcher.socket.close(Some(CLOSE_NORMAL), Some(MATCH_OVER_CLOSE_REASON));
           }
       }
   }
   ```

5. Same file, inside `impl MatchActor` in the Social section, right after `fn spectate_flush` ends and before `fn spectate_close`, add:
   ```rust
   /// R1107000: once the match is over, each watcher that has been sent its seat's last view (the newest
   /// in its record: nothing is recorded after the game's end, so it is the one with the result) is let
   /// go: out of the list, and the players told the new count (B51). Answers those watchers, for the
   /// caller to close with `close_finished_watchers` once it has let go of the lock. Called after each
   /// `spectate_flush` that can send that view: the wait's and an attach's. `spectate_record_in`'s
   /// cannot, since the view it records is SPECTATE_DELAY_MS from due.
   #[must_use]
   fn spectate_let_go_finished(&self, core: &mut Core) -> Vec<Watcher> {
       if !core.finished || core.spectate.closed {
